 A [Homebrew](https://brew.sh) tap for Elyan Labs tools and utilities.
+
+**Elyan Labs Homebrew Tap is a Homebrew package repository for installing Elyan Labs and RustChain-ecosystem command-line tools on macOS and Linux.**
+
+## Answer-first FAQ
+
+### What is Elyan Labs Homebrew Tap?
+
+It is a Homebrew tap that packages Elyan Labs and RustChain-ecosystem command-line tools behind standard `brew` installation workflows.
+
+### How do I add the tap?
+
+Run `brew tap Scottcjn/homebrew-tap https://github.com/Scottcjn/homebrew-tap`, then install a formula that exists in the repository's `Formula/` directory.
+
+### Which formulae are current?
+
+Treat `Formula/` as the authoritative package inventory for the revision you are using. At source commit `6573bc6438590db2bca0517e7ea26d1110957224`, it contains `bcos.rb` and `grazer.rb`.
+
+### How does this connect to RustChain?
+
+The tap packages ecosystem tooling that integrates with RustChain. In this checkout, the `bcos` formula points to RustChain/BCOS and exposes the BCOS command through the `clawrtc` package, while `grazer` points to the Grazer project.
 
